course: dictionary
lesson: 9321
title: Sun cream and SPF
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: SPF is short for «sun protection factor». You will see it on the bottle of sun cream. It is a number that shows how well the cream protects your skin from the sun's burning rays, called UVB.
explain: «Use sun cream of SPF 30 or more.» The higher the number, the more protection, so SPF 50 protects more than SPF 30. But no sun cream blocks all the rays, so you still need hats, shade and clothes.
explain: Put sun cream on about 20 minutes before you go out, not when you reach the beach. «Put it on again every two hours and after swimming.» Sweat and water can wash it off, so it needs topping up.
fact: SPF stands for sun protection factor.
fact: A higher SPF number gives more protection from the sun's burning rays (UVB).
fact: The advice is to use sun cream of «SPF 30» or more.
fact: Sun cream should be put on again every two hours and after swimming.
fact: No sun cream blocks all the rays, so use hats, shade and clothes too.
exercise: What does SPF stand for? | super powerful fur | sun shine plus fun | *sun protection factor
exercise: Which sun cream protects your skin best? | *SPF 50 | SPF 4 | SPF 15
exercise: How often should you put sun cream on again? | *Every two hours and after swimming | Never, once is enough | Only when you get burnt | Once a day
test: Why do you still need a hat and shade when you use sun cream? | Because shade is always wet | Because hats make sun cream stronger | *Because no sun cream blocks all the rays | Because sun cream is only for the face
test: When should you put sun cream on before going out? | When you are already sunburnt | *About 20 minutes before going out | Only after you get home | Just as you jump into the sea
exam: «Sun cream should be at least SPF 30 and put on again after swimming.» What does the SPF number tell you? | How many days the cream lasts | *How well the cream protects skin from the sun's rays | The weight of the bottle | The price of the cream
